From b832d42b790f6fac81180bf9d18227fa8811228f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 14:50:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 50/51] begonia-wifi (fwport): strip BEG bring-up debug
 scaffolding

Remove my own bring-up instrumentation now that WiFi works:
 - begtrace.h: MMIO-hijack oracle (#undef/redefine readl/writel/udelay/
   CONSYS_REG_* to pr_err every access) - was included nowhere, delete.
 - begsnap.h + begtrace_rx_snapshot(): conn RX-DMA/WFSYS/mailbox register
   dumper; remove the 3 includes + 5 call sites (+ their debug comments).
 - stp_exp.c sys_if_tx: drop the [BEGTRACE_TX] hexdump, the if= print, and
   the [BEGTRACE_CONN]/[BEGTRACE_PC] ioremap/readl probe block; keep the
   real UART/SDIO/BTIF transport dispatch verbatim.
No functional change. Verified on HW (running .ko md5 79201088): 0 BEGTRACE
in module+dmesg, WIFI function ON, wlan0 scans 2.4+5GHz. -153 LOC.
